WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.000
ProvenSky — Plan it. Prove it. Fly it. By БОГMODE.

2
00:00:03.001 --> 00:00:06.001
Plan · Pemby round flight, Winnipeg: one drone, 20
inspection points, three zones.

3
00:00:06.001 --> 00:00:10.285
Four steps: area, drones, mission type, check.

4
00:00:10.285 --> 00:00:14.103
The verdict chip opens the rules check: 1 action — NAV
Drone authorization for the CYWG control zone.

5
00:00:14.103 --> 00:00:18.103
Notes keep the rest in view: an antenna site nearby (ISED
tower data), terrain not yet checked.

6
00:00:18.683 --> 00:00:23.683
Load NRCan terrain: ground 228–233 m. The surface model
flags a low-clearance spot to verify on site.

7
00:00:27.713 --> 00:00:32.713
Prepare NAV Drone request: the plan fills in the area,
altitude and aircraft; the pilot adds the rest.

8
00:00:33.245 --> 00:00:37.845
Example details only. The area exports as KML and GeoJSON
for the NAV Drone portal; the pilot submits it.

9
00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:42.800
Simulate · 3D replay of the plan at 16×, overview first…

10
00:00:42.942 --> 00:00:47.142
…then the camera follows the drone along the route.

11
00:00:48.628 --> 00:00:52.573
Review · the Godot run took 453 s vs 301 s planned
(flagged) and used 28.6% of the pack.

12
00:00:52.573 --> 00:00:57.573
50-run wind test, real Godot runs in varied wind: 50 of 50
passed; worst waypoint error 0.06 m, max pack 31%.

13
00:00:57.772 --> 00:01:02.772
Real-flight compare, waypoint by waypoint. No Pemby flight
yet: this sample log is a simulated run.

14
00:01:03.878 --> 00:01:06.480
Export the evidence pack: plan, rules check, weather,
terrain, sim and flight results in one PDF.

15
00:01:06.480 --> 00:01:13.880
6 pages for an SFOC application, a client or an insurer.
Decision support, not an authorization.

16
00:01:13.897 --> 00:01:18.337
Fly · on the phone: go/no-go stays No-go until the NAV
Drone authorization is recorded.

17
00:01:18.337 --> 00:01:21.737
Then the pre-flight checklist, item by item.

18
00:01:21.760 --> 00:01:25.760
Founding operators wanted — bogmode.ca/provensky
